
<subsection xml:id="subsec-local-variables">










<p>
      In the <c>HelloWorld</c> class (<xref ref="lstng_helloworld"></xref>),
      the instance variable <c>greeting</c>
      (line 8) stores a value of type <c>String</c>. In the <c>main()</c> method,
      the variable <c>helloworld</c> is assigned a <c>HelloWorld</c> object
      (line 16).
</p>









<p>Try running the program below.</p>

<activity label="AsgnEx">
<statement><p>Run the following code. 
    Click on the "Show Code Lens" button and then the Next button to step through the code.</p></statement>
<program language="java" interactive="activecode"><input>
public class AsgnEx 
{                                   
     public static void main(String[] args)
     {
        int num1, num2;   // Declare the variables in memory
        num1 = 50;        // (a) Assign 50 to num1
        num2 = 10 + 15;   // (b) Assign 25 to num2
        num1 = num2;      // (c) Copy num2's value (25) into num1
        System.out.println("num1 is " + num1 + " and num2 is " + num2);
      }
}            
</input></program></activity>

</p>




<exercises>
<title>Self-Study Exercises</title>


      <exercise label="assignmentEx1">
            <title>Fill-In, Assignment statements</title>
      
            <statement>
                  <p>The variable <c>num</c> will have the value <var/> after the following two statements are executed:
                        <program language="java"><input>
                              int num = 11;
                              num = 23 - num;
                         </input></program>
                  </p>
            </statement>
            <setup>
                  <var>
                        <condition string="12">
                              <feedback>
                                    <p>Correct, 23 - 11 is 12, which is stored in <c>num</c>.</p>
                              </feedback>
                        </condition>
                        <condition string=".*">
                              <feedback>
                                    <p>Incorrect. Did you perform the subtraction on the right hand side?</p>
                              </feedback>
                        </condition>
                  </var>
            </setup>
      <solution><p> The value 12 is stored in <c>num</c>. 
      </p></solution>
      </exercise>

      <exercise label="assignmenEx2">
            <title>Fill-In, Assignment statements</title>
            <statement>
                  <p> Write a statement that will declare an <c>int</c> variable 
                        named <c>num2</c> and assigns 
                        it an initial value of 0: <var/>.
                  </p>
            </statement>
            <setup>
                  <var>
                        <condition string="int num2 = 0;">
                              <feedback>
                                    <p>Correct.</p>
                              </feedback>
                        </condition>
                        <condition string=".*">
                              <feedback>
                                    <p>Incorrect.</p>
                              </feedback>
                        </condition>
                  </var>
            </setup>
            <solution>
                  <p>
                        <c>int num2 = 0;</c>
                      </p>
            </solution>
      </exercise>

</exercises>





</subsection>





